# The ladder checkpoints are append-only logs, written on more than one
# machine at once: tools/rung.sh appends a row as each cube lands, and a
# session may be editing the header at the same time. Union merge keeps
# both sides' rows instead of raising a conflict over a file where every
# line is independent data.
#
# Union merge can leave a duplicate row if two machines decide the same
# cube. That is harmless -- the rows agree, and rung.sh's skip test reads
# the first match -- but `sort -u` on the data lines tidies it.
docs/ladder/*.tsv merge=union
